language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ csplib_007_all_interval: an Essence' model from DCP Rosetta.
$
$ Given the n pitch-classes 0, 1, ..., n-1, find a series x = (x_1, ..., x_n) in which each pitch-class occurs exactly once, and in which the intervals between neighbouring notes, |x_(i+1) - x_i|, are exactly the values 1, 2, ..., n-1, each occurring once. That is, the series is a permutation of 0 to n-1 and its interval vector is a permutation of 1 to n-1.
$
$ Save this file as model.eprime. Download `csplib_007_all_interval.json` and `dcp_convert_essence.py` from the
$ problem's page:
$   https://dcp-bench.github.io/DCP-Rosetta/problems/csplib_007_all_interval.html
$ Convert the instances once, then run the first one with Savile Row 1.11 (it needs Java); the
$ solution is written to `csplib_007_all_interval_1.param.solution`:
$   python dcp_convert_essence.py csplib_007_all_interval.json
$   savilerow model.eprime csplib_007_all_interval_1.param -run-solver

$ n: the number of pitch-classes
given n : int(2..)

$ x[i]: the pitch-class at position i of the series (indices 1-based, values 0 to n-1)
find x : matrix indexed by [int(1..n)] of int(0..n-1)
$ diffs[i]: the interval between the neighbouring notes at positions i and i+1, the absolute difference, values 1 to n-1
find diffs : matrix indexed by [int(1..n-1)] of int(1..n-1)

such that
$ each pitch-class 0 to n-1 occurs exactly once in the series
allDiff(x),
$ each interval is the absolute difference of two neighbouring pitch-classes
forAll i : int(1..n-1) . diffs[i] = |x[i+1] - x[i]|,
$ each interval from 1 to n-1 occurs exactly once among the intervals
allDiff(diffs)
